<title>UK: Boots shares up ahead of trading result.</title>
<headline>Boots shares up ahead of trading result.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in British healthcare and general retailer Boots Co Plc rose to near-record levels on Monday ahead of the group's first quarter trading statement, analysts said.</p>
<p>Shares in Boots ended the session 11 pence higher at  825 pence, close to a peak of 827 pence, ignoring falls elsewhere.</p>
<p>One trader said the market was &quot;pleasantly surprised&quot; by the rise in Boots.</p>
<p>He said the market may have been acting defensively following a better-than-expected trading statement by Marks &amp; Spencer Plc last week.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
